{"text": "The targeted tests now reach glom’s CLI, and FunctionBuilder works on the sandbox’s Python version. I also found and fixed defects in reverse subtraction and the fast ordered multidict’s handling of repeated keys. Next I’ll address the missing glom spec types and test their composition. Some existing tests have unrelated Python 3.12 compatibility failures; I’ll report those separately.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_aLk4wt80XHCneJAnDsRg7f5C", "name": "repo__shell", "arguments": {"command": "python - <<'PY'\np='consumer/glom/core.py';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace('ret = scope[Inspect](target, self.wrapped, scope)','ret = scope[Inspect](target, spec, scope)')\n# Modes apply only to ordinary specs. Specifier objects and T always dispatch first.\ns=s.replace(\"    elif isinstance(spec, dict):\\n        return _handle_dict(target, spec, scope)\",\"    elif scope.get(_MODE) is Fill:\\n        return _fill(target, spec, scope)\\n    elif isinstance(spec, dict):\\n        return _handle_dict(target, spec, scope)\")\nstart=s.index('\\n\\nclass _AbstractIterable(')\ns=s[:start]+'''\n\n_MODE = make_sentinel('_MODE')\n\n\nclass Auto(object):\n    \"\"\"Evaluate *spec* using glom's normal path and transformation semantics.\n\n    Use Auto inside Fill to opt a subexpression back into normal evaluation.\n    The selected mode is local to the wrapped specification.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, spec=T):\n        self.spec = spec\n\n    def glomit(self, target, scope):\n        scope[_MODE] = Auto\n        return scope[glom](target, self.spec, scope)\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return '%s(%r)' % (type(self).__name__, self.spec)\n\n\nclass Fill(Auto):\n    \"\"\"Build a template from literals, evaluating T and specifier objects.\n\n    Unlike ordinary glom specs, strings are literals and tuples and lists\n    construct containers rather than pipelines or iteration specifications.\n    Callables still receive the current target.\n    \"\"\"\n    def glomit(self, target, scope):\n        scope[_MODE] = Fill\n        return scope[glom](target, self.spec, scope)\n\n\ndef _fill(target, spec, scope):\n    recurse = lambda subspec: scope[glom](target, subspec, scope)\n    if isinstance(spec, dict):\n        return type(spec)((recurse(key), recurse(value))\n                          for key, value in spec.items())\n    if isinstance(spec, (list, tuple, set, frozenset)):\n        return type(spec)(recurse(value) for value in spec)\n    if callable(spec):\n        return spec(target)\n    return spec\n\n\nclass Let(object):\n    \"\"\"Bind named subspec results in the current scope, passing target through.\n\n    Bindings are accessible to subsequent specs through :data:`S` and remain\n    local to the enclosing evaluation (including individual iteration items).\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, **bindings):\n        self.bindings = bindings\n\n    def glomit(self, target, scope):\n        values = {name: scope[glom](target, spec, scope)\n                  for name, spec in self.bindings.items()}\n        scope.maps[1].update(values)\n        return target\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return 'Let(%s)' % ', '.join('%s=%r' % item\n                                    for item in self.bindings.items())\n''' + s[start:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='consumer/glom/__init__.py';s=open(p).read().replace('                       Check,','                       Check,\\n                       Auto,\\n                       Fill,\\n                       Let,');s+='\\nfrom glom.streaming import Iter, First\\n';open(p,'w').write(s)\np='consumer/glom/cli.py';s=open(p).read().replace('yaml.load(target_text)','yaml.safe_load(target_text)');open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY", "timeout_s": 10}}], "usage": {"input_tokens": 3, "cache_read_tokens": 24142, "cache_write_tokens": 956, "output_tokens": 1460, "reasoning_tokens": 516, "source": "provider", "prompt_tokens": 25101, "completion_tokens": 1460}, "model": "openai/gpt-6.1-sol", "finish": "tool_calls", "